+## Changed
+- Ported TypeScript's recertification branch into Rust retry: `marker::recertification` now selects a scope regression with a recorded done hash instead of refusing it; `retry::finish` branches to a new `recertify` orchestrator.
+- Added `scope.rs` for `resolveScope`/`computeTaskScopeHash`, `yaml.rs` for the marker rewrite, `excerpt.rs` for `tailVerifyOutput`, and `recertify/fields.rs` for differing paths, attribution and the done-marker refresh.
+- Recertification reads the task through `read_task_file`, loads config, runs the task verify via `run_verify` with the absolute change folder, writes the `recertification` event, retains the regressed marker and queues the done marker on failure, and prints the `Recertified`/`Requeued` lines.
+- Reused the existing retain and event-append steps in `record.rs`, added the new output text to `text.rs`, and removed the old recertification refusal.
+- Added `osq-kernel-harnesses`, `sha2` and `yaml-rust2` to the crate manifest, and updated the `11`, `1` refusal row to the missing-task error.
+- Copied the recert fixture and goldens unchanged and added `tests/retry_recert.rs` for the four new scenarios plus output-tail boundary cases.
+
+## Deviated
+- `Cargo.lock` was rewritten by cargo for the three new crate dependencies. The task scope lists only `crates/features/retry/**`, but the dependencies cannot land without the lock update; the workspace's lock-file rule lets `Cargo.lock` follow the covered `crates/features/retry/Cargo.toml`.
+- The scope resolver walks the project once per pattern rather than stopping at the pattern's search root. This is behaviorally identical because `scope_covers_path` filters every candidate, and it keeps the out-of-project pattern cases at no results without an extra optimization branch.
+
+## Missing context
+- The task scope omitted the root `Cargo.lock` even though the acceptance line requires the three new crate dependencies.
